+# Contract: Command-line interface
+
+**Feature**: `001-pastebin-service` | **Date**: 2026-11-20
+
+The operator-facing interface. Fixed by the spec (FR-025…FR-030) — invocation, readiness line,
+stream discipline, and exit statuses are contractual.
+
+---
+
+## Invocation
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m pastebin serve --port PORT --data DIR
+```
+
+| Element | Required | Constraints |
+|---|---|---|
+| `serve` | yes | The only subcommand |
+| `--port PORT` | yes | Integer `1 … 65535` |
+| `--data DIR` | yes | Path to the storage directory; created with parents if absent |
+
+`python -m pastebin` requires `src/` on `PYTHONPATH` (spec assumption); the package exposes
+`src/pastebin/__main__.py` for this.
+
+---
+
+## Success behaviour
+
+1. `DIR` is created if missing, including missing parents (FR-026); an existing directory is
+   used as-is with its pastes intact (FR-028).
+2. Each unreadable or unrecognised entry in `DIR` is reported on **stderr** and skipped;
+   startup continues (FR-032).
+3. The listening socket is bound to `127.0.0.1:PORT` and is accepting connections (FR-025).
+4. Exactly one line is written to **stdout** and flushed (FR-027):
+
+   ```text
+   listening on 127.0.0.1:8080
+   ```
+
+5. Requests are served until the process is terminated. A request sent immediately after the
+   readiness line is served, not refused (FR-027, R-002).
+
+Exit status `0` is returned only on a clean shutdown (`SIGINT`/`SIGTERM`).
+
+---
+
+## Stream discipline (FR-030)
+
+| Stream | Content |
+|---|---|
+| `stdout` | the readiness line, and nothing else |
+| `stderr` | every diagnostic: startup failures, skipped storage entries, per-request access/error logs |
+
+The two are never interleaved on one stream. In particular, `BaseHTTPRequestHandler`'s request
+logging goes to stderr, so a test can parse stdout for the readiness line alone.
+
+---
+
+## Failure behaviour (FR-029)
+
+Every startup failure prints a specific diagnostic to **stderr**, exits **non-zero** (`2`), and
+prints no readiness line and serves no request.
+
+| Condition | Exit | Diagnostic (shape) |
+|---|---|---|
+| `serve` subcommand missing or unknown | `2` | `argparse` usage error |
+| `--port` missing | `2` | `argparse`: `the following arguments are required: --port` |
+| `--data` missing | `2` | `argparse`: `the following arguments are required: --data` |
+| `--port` not an integer (`--port abc`) | `2` | names the invalid `--port` value |
+| `--port` out of range (`0`, `-1`, `65536`, `99999`) | `2` | names the valid range `1-65535` |
+| `--data` cannot be created (e.g. a parent is a file) | `2` | names the path and the OS reason |
+| `--data` exists but is not writable | `2` | names the path and that it is not writable |
+| `--data` exists but is not a directory | `2` | names the path |
+| `PORT` already in use | `2` | names the address and that it is in use |
+
+Diagnostics for hand-detected failures are prefixed `pastebin: ` (R-013). No failure path
+returns `0`, and no failure path prints to stdout (Constitution II).
+
+---
+
+## Examples
+
+### Create, read raw, miss (the three documented examples, SC-010)
+
+```bash
+$ PYTHONPATH=src python -m pastebin serve --port 8080 --data /tmp/pastes &
+listening on 127.0.0.1:8080
+
+$ curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/pastes \
+    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+    -d '{"content": "hello"}'
+{"id": "A1b2C3d4E5f6G7h8I9j0K_", "delete_token": "7Hq2...", "url": "/pastes/A1b2C3d4E5f6G7h8I9j0K_"}
+
+$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/pastes/A1b2C3d4E5f6G7h8I9j0K_/raw
+hello
+
+$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/pastes/nope
+{"error": "paste not found"}
+```
+
+### A failed start
+
+```bash
+$ PYTHONPATH=src python -m pastebin serve --port 99999 --data /tmp/pastes
+pastebin: --port must be an integer between 1 and 65535, got 99999
+$ echo $?
+2
+```
