+# Contract: HTTP API
+
+**Feature**: `001-pastebin-service` | **Date**: 2026-11-20
+
+The external interface of the service. This is the authoritative contract — the on-disk record
+format is not part of it (see [data-model.md](../data-model.md)).
+
+**Base**: `http://127.0.0.1:<port>` (loopback only, FR-025)
+
+**Defined routes** — every other method/path combination is `404` (FR-020):
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST` | `/pastes` | Create a paste |
+| `GET` | `/pastes/<id>` | Read a paste as JSON |
+| `GET` | `/pastes/<id>/raw` | Read a paste's content as plain text |
+| `DELETE` | `/pastes/<id>` | Delete a paste (requires `X-Delete-Token`) |
+
+**Global rules**
+
+- Query strings are ignored for routing: `/pastes/<id>?x=1` resolves to that paste (spec edge
+  case).
+- Every error response (`400`, `403`, `404`, `413`) has body `{"error": "<message>"}` with
+  `Content-Type: application/json` (FR-022).
+- `204` is the only response with no body and no `Content-Type` (FR-013).
+- `<id>` must match `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}$`; otherwise `404` with no filesystem access
+  (FR-023).
+- A request body larger than **1,048,576 bytes** (`Content-Length`) is refused `413` before the
+  body is read (FR-024, R-003).
+- Responses are HTTP/1.1 and always carry an explicit `Content-Length`.
+
+---
+
+## POST /pastes — create
+
+### Request
+
+```http
+POST /pastes HTTP/1.1
+Content-Type: application/json
+Content-Length: 17
+
+{"content": "hello"}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Constraints |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `content` | string | yes | ≤ 65,536 bytes UTF-8 encoded (inclusive); `""` is valid |
+| `expires_in` | integer | no | `1 … 2592000` inclusive; absent means never expires |
+
+Unknown fields are ignored (FR-007). `Content-Type` is not validated — the body is parsed as
+JSON regardless.
+
+### Response 201 Created
+
+```http
+HTTP/1.1 201 Created
+Content-Type: application/json
+
+{"id": "A1b2C3d4E5f6G7h8I9j0K_",
+ "delete_token": "7Hq2…",
+ "url": "/pastes/A1b2C3d4E5f6G7h8I9j0K_"}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` | string | 22 URL-safe chars; unique across everything the directory has ever held (FR-002) |
+| `delete_token` | string | 43 URL-safe chars; returned **here only**, never by a read route (FR-003) |
+| `url` | string | Exactly `"/pastes/" + id` (FR-001) |
+
+### Errors
+
+| Status | Cause | Requirement |
+|---|---|---|
+| `400` | body is not valid JSON | FR-004 |
+| `400` | body is absent / empty / no `Content-Length` | FR-004 |
+| `400` | body is valid JSON but not an object (`"x"`, `[1,2]`, `null`, `42`) | FR-004 |
+| `400` | `content` missing | FR-004 |
+| `400` | `content` is not a string | FR-004 |
+| `400` | `expires_in` present and not an integer (string, float, boolean, `null`) | FR-006 |
+| `400` | `expires_in` is `0`, negative, or `> 2592000` | FR-006 |
+| `400` | `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` (service requires `Content-Length`) | FR-004, R-003 |
+| `413` | `content` exceeds 65,536 UTF-8 bytes | FR-005 |
+| `413` | `Content-Length` exceeds 1,048,576 | FR-024 |
+
+No paste is stored when a creation request is rejected (FR-008).
+
+---
+
+## GET /pastes/{id} — read as JSON
+
+### Response 200 OK
+
+```http
+HTTP/1.1 200 OK
+Content-Type: application/json
+
+{"id": "A1b2C3d4E5f6G7h8I9j0K_",
+ "content": "hello",
+ "created_at": "2026-11-20T09:15:00Z",
+ "expires_at": null}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` | string | The requested identifier |
+| `content` | string | Byte-for-byte what was submitted (FR-012) |
+| `created_at` | string | `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`, UTC, whole seconds (FR-010) |
+| `expires_at` | string \| null | Same format, or `null` when the paste never expires (FR-010) |
+
+`delete_token` is **never** present in this body (FR-003).
+
+### Errors
+
+| Status | Cause | Requirement |
+|---|---|---|
+| `404` | identifier was never issued | FR-020 |
+| `404` | paste was deleted | FR-016 |
+| `404` | paste is expired (`now >= expires_at`) | FR-018 |
+| `404` | identifier fails the id shape check (`..`, `/`, `%2F`, absolute path) | FR-023 |
+| `404` | stored record is unreadable or of an unrecognised version (also reported on stderr) | FR-032 |
+
+---
+
+## GET /pastes/{id}/raw — read as plain text
+
+### Response 200 OK
+
+```http
+HTTP/1.1 200 OK
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
+Content-Length: 5
+
+hello
+```
+
+The body is the content and nothing else — no trailing newline is added, and an empty paste
+yields a zero-length body (FR-011, FR-012).
+
+### Errors
+
+Identical to `GET /pastes/{id}`: all cases above answer `404` with a JSON error body.
+
+---
+
+## DELETE /pastes/{id} — delete
+
+### Request
+
+```http
+DELETE /pastes/A1b2C3d4E5f6G7h8I9j0K_ HTTP/1.1
+X-Delete-Token: 7Hq2…
+```
+
+### Response 204 No Content
+
+No body, no `Content-Type` (FR-013). The paste is immediately unreadable by every route
+(FR-016).
+
+### Errors
+
+| Status | Cause | Requirement |
+|---|---|---|
+| `403` | paste exists and is unexpired, but `X-Delete-Token` is absent | FR-014 |
+| `403` | paste exists and is unexpired, but the header is empty | FR-014 |
+| `403` | paste exists and is unexpired, but the token does not match | FR-014 |
+| `403` | the supplied token is another paste's valid token | FR-014 |
+| `404` | identifier was never issued — **with any token or none** | FR-021 |
+| `404` | paste was already deleted — even with the original token | FR-021 |
+| `404` | paste is expired — even with the correct token | FR-018, FR-021 |
+| `404` | identifier fails the id shape check | FR-023 |
+
+**Ordering is contractual**: existence and expiry are resolved *before* the token is examined,
+so `404` always takes precedence over `403` and no response reveals whether an identifier
+exists (FR-021). A `403` leaves the paste retrievable (FR-014). Token comparison is
+constant-time (FR-015).
+
+---
+
+## Not-found catch-all
+
+`404` with a JSON error body, for example (FR-020, spec edge cases):
+
+| Request | Reason |
+|---|---|
+| `GET /` | undefined path |
+| `GET /pastes` | no listing route exists |
+| `DELETE /pastes` | undefined method for this path |
+| `PUT /pastes/<id>`, `PATCH /pastes/<id>` | undefined method on a defined path |
+| `POST /pastes/<id>` | undefined method on a defined path |
+| `GET /pastes/<id>/` | trailing slash |
+| `GET /pastes//raw` | empty identifier |
+| `GET /pastes/<id>/raw/extra` | `raw` is the only sub-resource |
+| `GET /pastes/<id>/anything` | undefined sub-resource |
+| `GET /pastes/../../etc/passwd` | id shape check (FR-023) |
+| `OPTIONS`, `HEAD`, or any other method on any path | undefined method |
+
+`405` is deliberately **not** used: the spec's rule is that anything outside the four defined
+routes is `404` (spec assumption).
+
+---
+
+## Status code summary
+
+| Status | When |
+|---|---|
+| `200` | successful `GET` of an existing unexpired paste (JSON or raw) |
+| `201` | successful creation |
+| `204` | successful deletion |
+| `400` | malformed JSON, missing/non-string `content`, invalid `expires_in`, missing body |
+| `403` | existing unexpired paste, bad or missing delete token |
+| `404` | unknown / deleted / expired paste, bad id shape, any undefined route or method |
+| `413` | `content` over 65,536 UTF-8 bytes, or request body over 1 MiB |
+
+## Robustness guarantee
+
+No request — malformed, oversized, hostile-path, unknown-route, or concurrent — causes the
+service to stop accepting further requests (SC-008). An unexpected internal defect is reported
+on stderr and answered `500` with the same JSON error shape; `500` is a backstop and is not a
+specified outcome of any documented input (R-011).
